            "heading_tag": "h2"
          }
        },
        "caption_K7BMNc": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "The Tuttle Twins and the Messed Up Market",
            "text_style": "large-semibold",
            "color_class": ""
          }
        },
        "text_ftnNVx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>After making some money, the twins decide to loan it out to other kids like them in order to earn some interest—and in the process learn about risk, bailouts, subsidies, and what happens when their children’s market gets messed up.This book is based on Human Action by Ludwig von Mises.</p>",
            "text_size": "regular",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        },
        "text_HXXxH8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Discover what makes the Tuttle Twins books different, and how they might fix the educational system we have today.</p>",
